  "reason": "Evidence: RNA encoder choice has shown a meaningful effect (scvi_n200: 0.520 vs pca_n2000: 0.485 in rna_only, a ~3.5% gap), and the current best multimodal result (config_039, 0.537) only marginally beats rna_only scvi_n200 (0.520), suggesting the RNA representation is the dominant signal source. Uncertainty: scgpt, a fundamentally different RNA encoder (masked-language-model based), has not been tested in any setting. Question: config_042 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) provides a clean one-variable comparison against config_009 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200), isolating the RNA encoder effect without confounding from image, fusion, or profile settings. Why best next: Completing the RNA-encoder ranking (scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000 vs scgpt) is the highest-information experiment because it determines which encoder to pair with image in subsequent multimodal tests. If scgpt substantially outperforms scvi_n200, the search direction shifts; if not, we can confidently exploit scvi_n200 in multimodal settings. This avoids changing multiple variables at once and directly reduces uncertainty about the most impactful design axis."
}

